## Step-by-Step Deployment

### Step 1: Generate Secrets
```bash
# Generate SECRET_KEY for backend
python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
```

### Step 2: Create .env Files
```bash
cp backend/.env.production backend/.env
cp frontend/.env.production frontend/.env

# Edit both files
nano backend/.env
nano frontend/.env
```

### Step 3: Fill in Your Values

| Value | Where to Find | Backend | Frontend |
|-------|---------------|---------|----------|
| Your Domain | Domain provider | API_URL, BOT_WEBHOOK_URL | VITE_API_URL |
| Telegram ID | @userinfobot | ADMIN_ID | VITE_ADMIN_ID |
| Bot Token | @BotFather | BOT_TOKEN | - |
| Database URL | DB provider | DATABASE_URL | - |
| Secret Key | Generated above | SECRET_KEY | - |

### Step 4: Deploy
```bash
docker-compose build --no-cache
docker-compose up -d
docker-compose logs -f
```

### Step 5: Register Telegram Webhook
```bash
curl -X POST https://api.telegram.org/bot<BOT_TOKEN>/setWebhook \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"url": "https://api.yourdomain.com/webhook/telegram"}'
```

### Step 6: Set Bot Mini App in @BotFather
- Chat with @BotFather
- `/mybots` → Your bot → `Bot Settings` → `Menu button` → `Web App`
- URL: `https://yourdomain.com`

